ription: Scroll to work section, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/#work\n\t\t\t\t\t\t29 text 2,900+ TESTS PASSING: FLAGSTONE REPORTED\n\t\t\t\t\t\t30 text 2026-08-16\n\t\t\t\t\t\t31 link Description: METHOD, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/#flagstone-test-count-method\n\t\t\t\t\t\t32 text 0 AXE VIOLATIONS: 17 ROUTES × 2 THEMES, STRICT RULES MEASURED\n\t\t\t\t\t\t33 text 2026-08-25\n\t\t\t\t\t\t34 link Description: EVIDENCE, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/accessibility/#receipts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t35 text V CALIBRATION ROUND, OPEN: 11 PHASES · 10 SHIPPED · 1 HELD REPORTED\n\t\t\t\t\t\t36 link Description: THE RECORD, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/colophon/#calibration\n\t\t\t\t\t37 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t38 text FEATURED: THE FLAGSHIP\n\t\t\t\t\t\t39 heading Flagstone, Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t40 text Flagstone\n\t\t\t\t\t\t41 text SEVERITY 3 OF 5 · MODERATE · VERIFIED Steep grade: a real barrier report expanded on the map. CURRENT EXPLORE SCREEN · FLAGSTONE STATUS App Store review submitted · August 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t42 link Description: VIEW PROJECT, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t43 image Flagstone's Explore map with an expanded verified Steep grade report, a real barrier photograph, orange map pins, map controls, and bottom navigation.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t44 text CURRENT PRODUCT CAPTURE · EXPLORE\n\t\t\t\t\t45 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t46 text THE SUPPORT WORK\n\t\t\t\t\t\t47 heading This is the job the projects come from., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t48 text This is the job the projects come from.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t49 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t50 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t51 text Lane 01 ESCALATION The escalation point for enterprise accounts.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t52 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t53 text Lane 02 TROUBLESHOOTING Compare cases to separate one-off user error from a repeatable pattern. Reproduce where possible, then isolate variables: app state, device behavior, account state, connectivity, workflow steps. The output is a likely cause, or the right escalation path.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t54 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t55 text Lane 03 DOCUMENTATION AND QA Reproducible steps, expected versus actual behavior, the conditions that matter, and any workaround or known limitation. Fixes and workflows get verified against the original support scenario and its nearby edge cases before anything is called resolved.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t56 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t57 text Lane 04 TRAINING Training and coaching teammates.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t58 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t59 text Lane 05 SUPPORT TO PRODUCT And the tools that fix it. Flagstone is the clearest case: accessibility software built because disabled people deserve navigation tools designed for them, not adapted for them.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t60 text NO METRICS HERE. EMPLOYER, ACCOUNT AND VOLUME DETAIL STAYS PRIVATE.\n\t\t\t\t\t61 text THE WORK\n\t\t\t\t\t62 heading A handful of things, made with intention., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t63 text A handful of things, made with intention.\n\t\t\t\t\t64 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t65 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t66 heading View Flagstone project, Value: 3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t67 link Description: View Flagstone project, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t68 text Community map of accessibility barriers: report a broken ramp, verify a neighbour's, see it marked fixed. Privacy-first: no ads, no analytics, no trackers.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t69 link Description: View project: Flagstone case study, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t70 link Description: FEATURED: ABOVE, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/#flagship\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t71 text 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t72 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t73 heading View Claude Corp project, Value: 3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t74 link Description: View Claude Corp project, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/claude-corp/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t75 text A governed multi-agent development system I designed and operate: 15 AI roles, a written Constitution, review gates, and autonomy bounded by explicit rules.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t76 link Description: View project: Claude Corp case study, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/claude-corp/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t77 text IN ACTIVE USE, ON MY PROJECTS ONLY 15 AI AGENTS\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t78 text 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t79 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t80 heading View Claude Corp Dashboard project, Value: 3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t81 link Description: View Claude Corp Dashboard project, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/dashboard/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t82 text The operator console for my agent team: what needs me, what is blocked, how each project is doing. Private in use; a public demo runs on synthetic data only.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t83 link Description: View project: Claude Corp Dashboard case study, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/dashboard/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t84 text PRIVATE OPERATOR APP · PUBLIC SYNTHETIC DEMO\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t85 text 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t86 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t87 heading View Prompt Library project, Value: 3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t88 link Description: View Prompt Library project, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/prompt-library/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t89 text Prompts as reusable assets, not scattered text: organize, search, fill variables, run. Kept in your browser; each run goes straight to Anthropic with your key.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t90 link Description: View project: Prompt Library case study, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/prompt-library/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t91 text LIVE AND EVOLVING · NO BACKEND OF MINE 100% STATIC\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t92 text 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t93 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t94 heading View Ghost Code project, Value: 3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t95 link Description: View Ghost Code project, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/ghost-code/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t96 text A terminal-command trainer and my first real build, made to get fluent in the command line and Claude Code. 56 cards, Arcade and Learn modes, no dependencies.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t97 link Description: View project: Ghost Code case study, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/ghost-code/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t98 text COMPLETE · LIVE · NO BACKEND 56 COMMAND CARDS\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t99 text 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t100 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t101 text THE RECORD\n\t\t\t\t\t\t102 heading The last thing I got wrong is in here too., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t103 text The last thing I got wrong is in here too.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t104 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t105 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t106 text Round V The Room: 11 phases · 10 shipped · 1 held · axe 0 violations · 34 scans  · \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t107 link Description: the record, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/colophon/#calibration\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t108 text OPEN\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t109 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t110 text Last defect the dead Report button : found by a simulator walk, fixed by one moved closing tag, re-proven by a test that fails against the old arrangement · \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t111 link Description: the account, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/#what-went-wrong\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t112 text CLOSED\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t113 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t114 text 2.2 AA the bar I build to:  pixel-contrast at the measured coordinates  · \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t115 link Description: the statement, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/accessibility/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t116 text 2026-08-25\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t117 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t118 text 100% focus stops visible: every tab stop, keyboard-traced  · \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t119 link Description: evidence, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/accessibility/#receipts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t120 text 2026-08-25\n\t\t\t\t\t121 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t122 text HOW THE WORK GETS MADE\n\t\t\t\t\t\t123 heading I direct AI agents, and I built the system that keeps them honest., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t124 text I direct AI agents, and I built the system that keeps them honest.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t125 text The projects above were implemented by AI agents working inside a governance system I designed: fifteen roles with explicit domain boundaries, and a written constitution that outranks any individual role or prompt. The agents do the implementation, the tests, and most of the diagnosis. I set the problem, make the architectural calls, and gate what lands. The constraints are what make the output reviewable. Database migrations are files with a rollback, never applied changes: no agent applies one to production, or sends anything outside the repository, without my explicit authorization under a narrow, mechanically gated exception. None handles credentials. Exactly one of the fifteen may message me; the rest write to files I read on my own schedule. Merges to\n\t\t\t\t\t\t126 text main\n\t\t\t\t\t\t127 text  are mine, with one narrow gated exception I granted to a single project. Here is the system working. An agent fixing something unrelated added two background-location permission strings to\n\t\t\t\t\t\t128 text app.json\n\t\t\t\t\t\t129 text . The privacy role blocked it: the app uses no background-location APIs, so declaring them would invite an App Store 5.1.1 rejection and ask for a permission the product does not need. Both keys were removed; neither reached\n\t\t\t\t\t\t130 text main\n\t\t\t\t\t\t131 text . And here is what it hands back. A review found that anonymous reports skipped a content filter that signed-in reports run. It was written up and deliberately left unpatched, because deciding what to filter on a submit form is a moderation policy, not a bug fix. It waited for me instead of being quietly patched, and the filter runs on both paths now. The honest limit: these fences are prompt-level, not sandbox-level. It is one person ’ s system, tested across one person ’ s projects, and some of the governance overhead does not pay for itself.\n\t\t\t\t\t132 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t133 text A BRIEF ACCOUNT\n\t\t\t\t\t\t134 heading The work is careful. The record is honest., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t135 text The work is careful. The record is honest.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t136 text One careful deliverable beats a dozen rough ones. Most of what I make starts with a problem worth solving. I prefer small, exact software to large, approximate software. I work from Canada , mostly on AI tooling, accessibility infrastructure, and the systems that make a product feel calm. I keep a written record of how each thing was made. The documentation is part of the deliverable, not an afterthought.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t137 link Description: THE FULL ACCOUNT, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/about/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t138 text Credentials, earned in order:  9  of them, with issuers and dates.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t139 link Description: See the credential badges, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/certificates/\n\t\t\t\t\t140 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t141 text LET’S TALK\n\t\t\t\t\t\t142 heading Have something worth building? Let’s talk about it., Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t143 text Have something worth building? Let’s talk about it.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t144 link Description: EMAIL ME, Value: mailto:hello@skypistudio.com?subject=Hello%20from%20your%20portfolio\n\t\t\t\t\t145 container The five works, on the horizon\n\t\t\t\t\t\t146 link Description: Flagstone: lit, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/flagstone/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t147 link Description: Claude Corp: lit, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/claude-corp/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t148 link Description: Claude Corp Dashboard: dark, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/dashboard/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t149 link Description: Prompt Library: lit, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/prompt-library/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t150 link Description: Ghost Code: lit, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/ghost-code/\n\t\t\t\t151 container\n\t\t\t\t\t152 link Description: Sky Halisky, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/\n\t\t\t\t\t153 text SMALL, EXACT SOFTWARE, DOCUMENTED HONESTLY. SKYPI STUDIO: EST. 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t154 heading SITE, Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t155 text SITE\n\t\t\t\t\t156 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t157 link Description: Home, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t158 link Description: The Work, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/work/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t159 link Description: Credentials, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/certificates/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t160 link Description: A Brief Account, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/about/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t161 link Description: Notes, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/blog/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t162 link Description: Accessibility, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/accessibility/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t163 link Description: Colophon, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/colophon/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t164 link Description: Let’s talk, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/contact/\n\t\t\t\t\t165 heading ABOUT, Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t166 text ABOUT\n\t\t\t\t\t167 text Sky Halisky  builds small, careful AI tools. Accessible by default, useful by design, so no one’s left out. Built in public, honest about what ships: every one of them live on the open internet.\n\t\t\t\t\t168 link Description: Full history on LinkedIn (opens in new tab), Value: linkedin.com/in/skyler-halisky\n\t\t\t\t\t169 heading ELSEWHERE, Value: 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t170 text ELSEWHERE\n\t\t\t\t\t171 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t172 link Description: Send email to hello@skypistudio.com, Value: mailto:hello@skypistudio.com\n\t\t\t\t\t\t173 link Description: GitHub (opens in new tab), Value: github.com/skypie99\n\t\t\t\t\t\t174 link Description: LinkedIn (opens in new tab), Value: linkedin.com/in/skyler-halisky\n\t\t\t\t\t175 text BUILT IN THE OKANAGAN VALLEY, BRITISH COLUMBIA. NO ANALYTICS. NO COOKIES.\n\t\t\t176 container Infobar Container\n\t\t\t\t177 container Infobar\n\t\t\t\t\t178 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t179 text Continue where you left off: Chromium restores your tabs every time you restart. To turn this off, go to\n\t\t\t\t\t\t180 link Settings, opens in new tab.\n\t\t\t\t\t181 button Close\n\t\t\t182 tab group\n\t\t\t\t183 pop up button Tab Search\n\t\t\t\t184 container\n\t\t\t\t\t185 tab (selected, settable, boolean) Description: Sky Halisky: Senior Technical Support, Value: on\n\t\t\t\t\t\t186 button Close\n\t\t\t\t187 button New Tab\n\t188 close button\n\t189 full screen button Help: this button also has an action to zoom the window, Secondary Actions: zoom the window\n\t190 minimize button\n191 menu bar\n\t192 Google Chrome for Testing\n\t193 File\n\t194 Edit\n\t195 View\n\t196 History\n\t197 Bookmarks\n\t198 Profiles\n\t199 Tab\n\t200 Window\n\t201 Help\n\nThe focused UI element is 70 link Description: FEATURED: ABOVE, Value: 127.0.0.1:4405/#flagship"